exit: 1
-- REFINEMENT ----------------- errors/old_misuse_1.march

`old(…)` cannot be used in an `@invariant`. [old_misuse]

2 |   @invariant(count >= old(count))
                          ^^^^^^^^^^

    `old(e)` means `e` of the state a message arrived with, so it is only meaningful in a handler's `ensures`: `on Msg(…) ensures state.n >= old(state.n) do … end`.
    run `march --explain old_misuse`


